:"2003-07-28","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may find a basic Forest or any land card with the land type Forest.","oracle_id":"78826359-fe63-44ad-adc4-a17ffcd710e4","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The Great Divide Guide is an Ally and gives its granted ability to itself.","oracle_id":"79e69a91-d580-47fb-be76-1e32c50d2fa0","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you've activated Resonating Lute's last ability, it doesn't matter if the number of cards in your hand drops below seven. The ability will still resolve as normal.","oracle_id":"9263287d-f782-4318-9ab8-e2e5f8107f5e","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A spell's mana value is determined only by its mana cost. Ignore any alternative costs, additional costs, cost increases, or cost reductions.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the discovered card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you can't cast the discovered card (perhaps because there are no legal targets for the spell), you'll put it into your hand.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a spell \"without paying its mana cost\", you can't choose to cast it for any alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs. If the spell has any mandatory additional costs, you must pay those to cast it.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you discover an adventurer card, split card, or modal double-faced card, you might be able to cast that card with either set of characteristics depending on the effect's discover value. For example, if you discover 4 and reveal Galvanic Giant (an adventurer card from Wilds of Eldraine with a mana value of 4), you could cast Galvanic Giant, but not Storm Reading (its Adventure, which has a mana value of 7). If you discover 7 and reveal Galvanic Giant, you could cast either Galvanic Giant or Storm Reading.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some spells and abilities that cause you to discover may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve and you won't discover.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The mana value of a split card is determined by the combined mana cost of its two halves. If discover allows you to cast a split card, you may cast either half (as long as its mana value is less than or equal to the effect's discover value) but not both halves.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When you discover, you must exile cards. The only optional part of the ability is whether you cast the exiled card or put it into your hand.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You exile the cards face up. All players will be able to see them.","oracle_id":"927979d7-9b5c-4448-aef0-baf2907a89f1","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A spell's mana value is determined only by its mana cost. Ignore any alternative costs, additional costs, cost increases, or cost reductions.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the discovered card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you can't cast the discovered card (perhaps because there are no legal targets for the spell), you'll put it into your hand.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast a spell \"without paying its mana cost\", you can't choose to cast it for any alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs. If the spell has any mandatory additional costs, you must pay those to cast it.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you discover an adventurer card, split card, or modal double-faced card, you might be able to cast that card with either set of characteristics depending on the effect's discover value. For example, if you discover 4 and reveal Galvanic Giant (an adventurer card from Wilds of Eldraine with a mana value of 4), you could cast Galvanic Giant, but not Storm Reading (its Adventure, which has a mana value of 7). If you discover 7 and reveal Galvanic Giant, you could cast either Galvanic Giant or Storm Reading.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some spells and abilities that cause you to discover may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve and you won't discover.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The mana value of a split card is determined by the combined mana cost of its two halves. If discover allows you to cast a split card, you may cast either half (as long as its mana value is less than or equal to the effect's discover value) but not both halves.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When you discover, you must exile cards. The only optional part of the ability is whether you cast the exiled card or put it into your hand.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You exile the cards face up. All players will be able to see them.","oracle_id":"a1c7cd7a-0795-4135-b787-effeb981d95b","published_at":"2023-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes Dress Down to become a creature, it will lose its own abilities along with all other creatures. This includes the triggered ability that causes it to be sacrificed at the beginning of the end step.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect grants a creature an ability after Dress Down has entered the battlefield, it won't lose that ability. For example, if a land becomes a creature while Dress Down is on the battlefield, it will still gain any abilities given to it by the effect that animated it. It will, however, lose any abilities it already had.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
